# split_sym_dim Pass Tests

- Test the pass by constructing the input program, running `split_sym_dim` plus required cleanup,
  constructing the complete expected program explicitly, and comparing them with
  `EXPECT(actual.sort() == expected.sort())`.
- Never call `program::compile`, `program::eval`, or create runtime parameter maps in this file.
- Do not replace the explicit expected graph with property checks or numerical assertions.
- Put numerical execution coverage in an appropriate `test/verify/` or target behavior test; it
  supplements but does not replace the structural pass test.
- Reuse the existing `add_clones` helper when expected split modules require it, while keeping each
  test's graph construction visible in the test case.
